{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664592-trying-to-understand-a-gift","id":664592,"title":"Trying to understand a gift","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-14T12:04:04-07:00","id":664592,"title":"Trying to understand a gift","content":"I'm trying to wrap my head around a Rank 3 Shadow Lord gift called &quot;Icy Chill of Despair&quot;. One of my players used it while being challenged by a slightly higher-ranking Silver Fang. The NPC rolled poorly, and according to the effect of the gift had to &quot;spend a Willpower point to attack, take action against or even verbally oppose the Shadow Lord&quot;.<br /> <br /> My player was under the impression that anyone subject to the gift would have to spend a point of willpower EACH TIME they wanted to oppose his character, thus quickly running NPCs out of their available WIllpower. It seems appropriately powerful for a Rank 3 gift, but we weren't sure as the text wasn't super specific. If the subjects can just spend a point of Willpower to counter a gift that costs Gnosis and a full turn of concentration, why even take it? Why wouldn't someone just spend the Willpower point if they failed? Is it my fault for assuming that even my low Willpower NPCs likely are sitting on at least three to four points they can spend as they choose? Is Willpower a far more precious resource than I had originally thought?<br /> <br /> Flavor-wise it makes sense, you become huge and intimidating which is a very neat effect, but Paralyzing Stare (also a Rank 3 Shadow Lord gift) does the intimidation game pretty damn well, too (with the added bonus of the target not being able to move). I'm trying really hard to reward this player (who has, in the past, been a bit of a powergaming monster and this new character is delightful and meshes with the rest of the group so nicely) but I'm also worried that if I allowed the gift to just drain opponents Willpower constantly it might be unbalancing.<br /> <br /> How would you have handled it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3766-convict24601","name":"Convict24601","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3766_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T12:29:45-07:00","id":664640,"title":"","content":"The gift is indeed unclear about that. I'd personally rule that one WP point is enough to completely overcome it.<br /> That being said, you've already noted that Paralyzing Stare seems stronger. The reason is simple: Paralyzing Stare affects one target. Icy Chill of Despair affects everyone in the vicinity.<br /> In a fight, every opponent starts combat one WP down (A Shadow Lord's Manipulation+Intimidation against 7 should generally beat an enemy's WP against 8).<br /> In a public debate, everyone who wants to speak out against the Lord only does so if it's worth a WP point to them. Imagine the scene: On a controversial, but not <i>hugely</i> important issue, the Shadow Lord argues against another Garou. How many &quot;Yeah, right!&quot;s is the other guy going to get from the audience if every one of those costs Willpower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T12:46:16-07:00","id":664648,"title":"","content":"That is... a really good point. We just weren't thinking BIG enough, and I can see some really devastating uses for his character (who happens to be a Galliard).<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3766-convict24601","name":"Convict24601","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3766_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T01:11:21-07:00","id":666610,"title":"","content":"Also Willpower is not that important until you run out of it, then you can't do anything until you regained a point in willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T19:33:22-07:00","id":667729,"title":"","content":"So here's my question...Willpower is important for a member of the changing breed (since if they run out they can no longer shift). But is there really any penalty for running out of will for any other critter (vampire, fomor, changeling, ect.)? aside that is from not being able to activate powers that take a will or getting an auto success on a roll. Because if there's no penalty there, then I don't really see how losing only 1 will in a battle is rank 3 worthy of an effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5268-tenrec","name":"Tenrec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T01:31:50-07:00","id":667991,"title":"","content":"In V20 your character becomes demotivated and is unable to do stuff except maybe basics like feeding. Your character will not come up with ideas and plans of its own nor will the act properly one threat that are non lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:48:21-07:00","id":668242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So here's my question...Willpower is important for a member of the changing breed (since if they run out they can no longer shift). </div> </div> </div>Actually, you need to run out of both Willpower and Rage to be unable to shift.<br /> <br /> All in all, I really don't like Vampire's way of treating temporary Willpower. Particularly the whole thing about Disciplines rolling against the temporary stat makes a roll that is already easy (=uncontested) almost trivial if the opponent uses disciplines that expend WP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because if there's no penalty there, then I don't really see how losing only 1 will in a battle is rank 3 worthy of an effect. </div> </div> </div>As I already noted, it's not &quot;only 1 will in a battle&quot; - it's 1 WP from every single opponent and it's every conceivable kind of direct opposition that requires the expenditure, including those that just aren't worth spending a WP on for every participant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:00:09-07:00","id":668324,"title":"","content":"I've only ever used it in social situations. Best one was while revealing the Shadow Lord NPC's big plan and all the incriminating evidence against her enemies, while they could only stare and fume. It can be very powerful that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:51:25-07:00","id":668769,"title":"","content":"By the way: I find this line of gifts to be an interesting illustration of the differing leadership strategies of Silver Fangs vs Shadow Lords. Silver Fangs make it so that having them as leader is the best option, because you then get stuff like Inspiration, Unity of the Pack and so on - Shadow Lords make opposing them more costly than just going along with their plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T19:46:36-07:00","id":695623,"title":"","content":"Another gift I have trouble understanding how POWERFUL is Ultimate Argument of Logic<br /> <br /> Does it ever wear off naturally? or can enough willpower spent degrade it?<br /> <br /> It says it makes you believe implicitly in something how differently is that from controlling behaviour if I make a young adult kinfolk woman uncomfortable with her Garou Fiance implicitly believe &quot;The bloodline of the Garou is sacred and blessed of Gaia, and nothing is more important then furthering it&quot; <br /> <br /> Does that neccessarily remove any problems she has or could it rebound in a odd way on the manipulative Theruge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-09-2015, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T02:02:22-07:00","id":695856,"title":"","content":"As written, Ultimate Argument of Logic is really powerful (it is a Rank 5 Gift after all). There's no expiration, or stated ability to degrade/resist it once it goes off. As long as it is one fact (your example is two facts, but could be rephrased easily enough), it works.<br /> <br /> The important bit here is, of course, that believing something is true doesn't remove any free will. Plenty of people believe, as a matter of implicit fact, that stealing is wrong; but still end up in situations where they steal something.<br /> <br /> In your example, the Theurge is actually kinda screwing it up if the goal is to make the kin go through with a relationship with a Garou she doesn't like. After all, she can believe in the importance of pumping out new Garou and Kin as strongly as anyone, while still finding a particular mate unworthy so she'll go find one that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T16:18:42-07:00","id":698043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664592-trying-to-understand-a-gift?p=695856#post695856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written, Ultimate Argument of Logic is really powerful (it is a Rank 5 Gift after all). There's no expiration, or stated ability to degrade/resist it once it goes off. As long as it is one fact (your example is two facts, but could be rephrased easily enough), it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. However, as an ST I am loathe to let something so unbalancing stand as is. For this, and certain other Gifts, I think it is best the ST determine a reasonable standard after taking into consideration the level of the Gift. Otherwise, it ends up making the game world too silly and erodes suspension of disbelief. Nothing in the Gift says the effects are permanent or that the belief is deeply held (not capable of being convinced by someone else that it is false). It just says the person is convinced something is fact, and people can be convinced later to believe other things even in non-magical ways.<br /> <br /> I would use a sliding time scale based on the improbability or deeply held belief of the target possibly combined with a Willpower expenditure. If a Theurge would use it to convince someone of something demonstratably false (such as the sun rises in the west), I'd have it last only one scene or at most until evidence of it comes up (seeing the sun rise at dawn). Target would not need to spend Willpower.<br /> <br /> In situations where the Theurge bamboozled the target (say a security guard letting in an unauthorized person into a facility), I'd give it a scene - maybe a bit longer taking into account nothing is going on wrong and the guard is getting coffee or something, but require the target to spend Willpower to realize, &quot;Omigawd, I shouldn't have let that person in&quot;. Length of time before the person realizes it may depend on the number of successes past the initial three.<br /> <br /> If there are things that are open to debate, but which directly contradict the target's values or convictions, I'd have it wear off in a day, week, or month at most with the target not needing to spend Willpower.<br /> <br /> If things are open to debate, but the target was unsure what was the truth (probably more philosophical questions), then the target would need to spend a Willpower after a certain amount of time to adopt another position.<br /> <br /> If the target wants to belief something what the Theurge is telling him (whether consciously or subconsciously), then the target may remain convinced indefinitely until something profound occurs which would cause him to challenge it. At which point, he's like anyone else pondering if something he's believed is actually true.<br /> <br /> The Storyteller system does not work well on strict game mechanics. It works best with a roleplay style that is much more freeform and then using checks and resource (Rage, Gnosis, Willpower, etc.) expenditure to resolve situations where there is reasonable doubt to outcome. The mechanics exist to support the story or game. STs should always exercise a reasonable interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T01:00:32-07:00","id":698452,"title":"","content":"I agree the Ultimate Argument of Logic is a bit borked. Though I'd rather have a more general house rule that applies to all mind-whammy powers.<br /> <br /> I personally love M20's &quot;I Disbelieve!&quot; chart, which basically lets targets roll Willpower against a variable difficulty based on how believable the mental illusion is, and they can break it after rolling 5 total successes during a scene. It seems like a great framework to develop a general cWOD anti-mind-whammy rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T16:37:39-07:00","id":700248,"title":"","content":"While I agree that the UAoL shouldn't be all-powerful (and I really wonder why it wasn't given to a more social auspice like Ragabash or Galliard), I'd also bear in mind that it's a Rank 5 gift, which is the level where Philodox can hand out Geasa, Silent Striders can teleport for hundreds of miles and Silver Fangs turn into living silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T04:46:49-07:00","id":700697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664592-trying-to-understand-a-gift?p=700248#post700248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that the UAoL shouldn't be all-powerful (and I really wonder why it wasn't given to a more social auspice like Ragabash or Galliard), I'd also bear in mind that it's a Rank 5 gift, which is the level where Philodox can hand out Geasa, Silent Striders can teleport for hundreds of miles and Silver Fangs turn into living silver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much that. Rank 5 is when your problems are way more complex then any gift, no matter how powerful could ever fix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}